1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,397
On Venus, one day lasts
longer than a whole year.

2
00:00:02,477 --> 00:00:04,332
Venus spins incredibly slowly.

3
00:00:04,332 --> 00:00:08,103
One full turn takes about two
hundred forty-three Earth days.

4
00:00:08,183 --> 00:00:10,690
That's slower than any other
planet in our solar system.

5
00:00:10,770 --> 00:00:12,891
But it circles the Sun
faster than Earth does.

6
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:16,675
One trip around the Sun takes only
two hundred twenty-five Earth days.

7
00:00:16,755 --> 00:00:19,444
So a single spin of Venus
outlasts its entire year.

8
00:00:19,524 --> 00:00:22,135
But here's the crazy part:
Venus spins backwards.

9
00:00:22,215 --> 00:00:25,254
It rotates the opposite way
from Earth and most other planets.

10
00:00:25,334 --> 00:00:28,444
So on Venus, the Sun rises
in the west and sets in the east.

11
00:00:28,524 --> 00:00:32,212
And under its thick clouds, it's so
hot that lead would melt into puddles.

12
00:00:32,292 --> 00:00:36,584
A day longer than a year, with sunrise
in the west. Follow for tomorrow's fact.

